import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About · Stop the Slop"
  description="What this library is, how an entry earns its place, and what the marks mean."
  current="about"
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1 data-slop-allow="color/multicolor-heading">About this document<span class="dot">.</span></h1>

    <p>
      Stop the Slop is a curated library of the efforts that push back against
      AI slop: the tools, field guides, standards, working groups, and journalism holding a
      line against the generated filler currently silting up design, writing, code, and images.
    </p>
    <p>
      It borrows its manners from two older documents. From the proofreader&rsquo;s leaflet:
      a notation system that says <em>someone read this closely and marked it</em>. From the
      1943 <em>Consumer Reports</em>: the nerve to print a named verdict,
      <span class="strike">Below&nbsp;Average</span> <span class="fix">Not&nbsp;Acceptable</span>,
      instead of hiding judgment behind stars.
    </p>

    <h2>How an entry earns its place</h2>
    <p>
      Somebody here has actually read, run, or used it. Every entry gets a short opinionated
      note (never a summary of the thing&rsquo;s own marketing), a verdict, and a
      <em>checked</em> date. Link libraries rot; the date is the promise that someone is
      still reading the proofs.
    </p>

    <h2>The marks</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>stet.</strong>, the proofreader&rsquo;s mark for &ldquo;let it stand&rdquo;:
      the original was right. Genuinely good; use it.<br />
      <strong>ok w/c</strong>, the press-proof marking for &ldquo;OK with
      corrections&rdquo;: useful, but read the caveat in the note.<br />
      <strong>kill.</strong>, the print-shop and newsroom term for copy that does not run:
      did not survive a close read.
    </p>

    <h2>What doesn&rsquo;t get in</h2>
    <p>
      Detection theater, slop laundering, and anything whose entire pitch is a percentage.
      A few of the worst offenders are cataloged anyway, under <strong>kill.</strong>
      The 1943 testing lab named the failing shoe; so do we.
    </p>

    <h2>Errata</h2>
    <p>
      Corrections, dead links, and nominations are welcome:
      <a href="https://github.com/laltaffer/stoptheslop/issues">submit an erratum</a>.
      The library is a public repository; every entry is a file anyone can read and contest.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
